  "prefLabel": "Mid 407.07 Compliance with Laws",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-11-08",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mid 407.07 Compliance with Laws. A midwife shall comply with applicable New Hampshire laws, including but not limited to:\n\n(a) The requirements of RSA 332-I relating to medical records and patient information;\n\n(b) Rules of the bureau of vital records regarding the reporting of births;\n\n(c) Rules of the bureau of vital records regarding the reporting of deaths;\n\n(d) The reporting requirements of RSA 132:6, II and any rules relating to prevention of eye inflammation which have been adopted by the commissioner of the department of health and human services; and\n\n(e) The requirements of RSA 132:10-a and RSA 132:10-aa relating to newborn screening tests.\n\nSource. #8840, eff 3-13-07, EXPIRED: 3-13-15\n\nNew. #11095, INTERIM, eff 5-12-16, EXPIRED: 11-8-16\n\nNew. #12040, eff 11-10-16\n\nAPPENDIX",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mid400.html"
